CHAPTER.VERS:
And Pilate went out again, and says to them, Look, I bring him out to you

          {+}
        , that you

          {+}
         may know that I find no crime in him.

Now it was the Preparation of the Passover: it was about the sixth hour. And he says to the Jews, Look, your

          {+}
         King!

They therefore cried out, Away with [him], away with [him], crucify him! Pilate says to them, Shall I crucify your

          {+}
         King? The chief priests answered, We have no king but Caesar.

And he who has seen has borne witness, and his witness is true: and he knows that he says true, that you

          {+}
         also may believe.
